// An allowlist, not a denylist. The denylist that stood here shipped 14 assessment artifacts
// from .sunstone/ into the VSIX, 2.5 MB carrying absolute home paths, the private register's
// content and shell commands from past sessions, because the rule only excluded what existed
// when it was written. Everything is excluded here and four things are named back in, so a new
// directory is out of the package by default rather than in it.
//
// vsce force-includes package.json and the README whatever this file says. It does NOT force-include
// LICENSE or CHANGELOG, and the first allowlist here dropped both: the extension is BUSL-1.1 and
// shipping it without its licence text is the defect C43 was about.
**

!out/extension.js
!media/**
!resources/**
!LICENSE
!CHANGELOG.md

// media/ is 12 MB on its own and is generated by scripts/sync-engine.sh; never edit it by hand.
!docs/GUIDE.md
!out/extension.js.map
